From 3f73258d8e3706d5a3568e9f038c502e086ec028 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aegis Development <development@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:32:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(android): revoke Access Options on primary document
 replacement

DevTools Page.setDocumentContent replaces the primary document through
Document::SetContent and the parameterless Document::open(). That path emits
neither DidOpenDocumentInputStream nor DidCommitDocumentReplacement. Notify
the browser from the explicit open so the existing editor is revoked. Ordinary
DOM edits do not reopen the document and stay readable.

Ordinary builds do not send that notification. The renderer IPC is compiled
only when internal Access Options are enabled. Blink and Chrome share one
declare_args in a Blink-visible gni, so the flag is not declared twice.

The explicit-open browser tests follow the same flag. Internal builds wait
for one notification. Ordinary builds idle and expect none, so a default
content_browsertests run does not time out. The javascript: replacement test
stays unconditional because it uses DidCommitDocumentReplacement().
